.TH YASH-EVENTSCTL 1 "July 2026" "yash-app-events 0.0.1"
.SH NAME
yash-eventsctl \- inspect and control yash-app-eventsd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yash-eventsctl
[--json] [--socket PATH] [--timeout-ms MS] COMMAND
.SH COMMANDS
version, status, state, shutdown, profile, events follow, capture, analyze PNG --profile-id UUID, replay MANIFEST,
catalog status/refresh/list/install, suite evaluate PACKAGE [--timings], collection policy/status/review/compare, output
list/set/enable/remove/test, diagnostic plan, and diagnostic export.
.PP
Profile validate and profile pack DIRECTORY ARCHIVE run offline. Pack validates a
portable profile directory and creates an inert .hudprofile archive for daemon import.
.PP
Diagnostic export requires an exact total returned by diagnostic plan plus the
--privacy-reviewed flag. Selected --element-id crops require a frozen preview.
.PP
Output routes are machine-local and profile-scoped. Direct-command routes require an
absolute executable, do not invoke a shell, and receive compact JSON on standard input.
.PP
Catalog refresh and install use the daemon-owned fixed GitHub Profile Catalog origin.
Install requires the reviewed catalog revision and SHA-256 and leaves the profile inactive.
.PP
Analyze returns scene-aware spatial JSON with frame dimensions, named element and target
rectangles, configured safe points, and crop-first AI handoff metadata. It never embeds
image bytes or generates input.
.PP
Suite evaluate omits unstable wall-clock data by default. --timings adds inventory,
profile-load, total-case, serialization, and ten-slowest-case millisecond diagnostics.
Use --progress, --detach, suite status, and suite cancel for long operations. Repeatable
--case/--category/--changed-fixture/--scene/--overlay/--element filters and --fail-fast
support authoring; --no-cache forces cold verification and --output atomically stores JSON.
.PP
Profile analyze-capacity PROFILE runs offline and reports shared limits, 80/90/100 percent
warnings, expensive detector families, unreachable/disabled-only elements, duplicate
configurations, per-scene cost estimates, and read-only consolidation suggestions.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 3 connection; 4 protocol/RPC; 5 validation; 6 timeout; 7 replay or suite regression.
.SH SEE ALSO
yash-app-eventsd(1)
